sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Pair a Linux host with Paws
    accDescr: A host creates a local key and enrolls over HTTPS. A recent administrator session approves the matching fingerprint. The host claims its certificate and uses mTLS for subsequent runner requests.
    participant H as Linux host
    participant P as Paws HTTPS enrollment
    participant U as Workspace administrator
    participant M as Paws mTLS listener
    H->>H: Generate private P-256 key and CSR
    H->>P: Name and CSR over HTTPS
    P-->>H: Pairing id, claim secret, code, fingerprint and expiry
    U->>P: Inspect code with recent owner/admin session
    U->>U: Compare fingerprint with host output
    U->>P: Approve pairing
    P->>P: Bind workspace and owner, sign certificate
    H->>P: Claim using pairing id and secret
    P-->>H: Runner/workspace identity, certificate and authority
    H->>M: Outbound TLS connection with client certificate
    M->>M: Verify certificate and current authorization
    M-->>H: Authenticated runner protocol
